<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Start here</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
    Tectonic Plates is a barbell log. It keeps what you lifted, works out what to load on
    the bar, and charts whether the weight is going up.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
    What makes it more than a list is that a session is written before it is trained: plan
    the week, then work off a screen at the rack that ticks each set off as you do it.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Three things worth doing first</h2>
  <%# Ordered by how soon each one pays back rather than by how much it does. Logging a
      single session takes a minute and gives the calendar and the charts something to
      say; writing a block is an evening's work; an assistant is worth little until there
      is training for it to read. %>
  <ol class="mt-3 space-y-4">
    <li class="rounded-lg bg-white p-4 shadow ring-1 ring-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Log a workout</h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
        Put in a date and the lifts you did, weight by weight. One session is enough for
        the calendar and the charts to have something to show.
      </p>
      <%# Full width on a phone and only as wide as its words from 640px up: a thumb
          reaching across a phone screen wants the whole line, and a mouse does not. %>
      <a href="/workouts/new"
         class="<%= button_style %> mt-3 inline-flex min-h-11 w-full items-center justify-center bg-lime-500 px-4 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-lime-600 sm:w-auto">Log a workout</a>
    </li>

    <li class="rounded-lg bg-white p-4 shadow ring-1 ring-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Write a training block</h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
        A block is weeks, each week days, each day the lifts you will do. The app turns a
        week of it into real sessions, warmup ramps and all, on the days you said.
      </p>
      <a href="/programs"
         class="<%= button_style %> mt-3 inline-flex min-h-11 w-full items-center justify-center bg-sky-800 px-4 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-sky-900 sm:w-auto">Write a block</a>
    </li>

    <li class="rounded-lg bg-white p-4 shadow ring-1 ring-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Connect an assistant</h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
        Give Claude or ChatGPT this account's address over MCP and it can plan a block, log
        a session, or correct a set you typed wrong. It sees your account and nothing else.
      </p>
      <a href="/connections"
         class="mt-3 inline-flex min-h-11 w-full items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-white px-4 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-inset ring-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50 sm:w-auto">Connect an assistant</a>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-500">
    Everything you log shows up on
    <a href="/" class="font-medium text-lime-600 hover:text-lime-500">the calendar</a>,
    which is the home page from here on.
  </p>
</div>
